<Routines>
<Routine Name="aaReadMe" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[/*]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[This routine describes how to run the sample project]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[Step1 - Home all the Axis to 0 degree position. See in routine “AbsPathMove_with_Multiple_WorkFrames”. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[Step2 - Set different Work Frames using Work Frame Offsets values. See offset values in “Work_Frame[]”array. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[Step3 - Setup MCTO with Cart_XYZRxRyRz as Cartesian System, Delta 4 axis as Robot System. Toggle  “Start_MCTO” tag to initiate MCTO. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[Step4 - Toggle “Start_PathMove” and start moving robot along the programmed path.  See absolute path position in “Path_Positions[]” array. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[Step5 - Change the Work Frame offsets and move the robot on the same path positions. See in routine “AbsPathMove_with_Multiple_WorkFrames”. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[Step6 - "Robot_TCP_Positions" routine computes TCP positions from Base frame using MCTPO with no Work Frame offsets. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[Step7 - Run Trends. See TCP XYZ position during the move with or without Work Frame offsets. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[*/]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="AbsPathMove_with_Multiple_WorkFrames" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(s:fs)MOV(0,WorkFrame_Index)MOV(1,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Home all the axis to 0-degree position.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MotionGroup.GroupSynced)EQU(step,1)MAH(J1,Mah_Ctr[0])MAH(J2,Mah_Ctr[1])MAH(J3,Mah_Ctr[2])MAH(J4,Mah_Ctr[3])XIC(Mah_Ctr[0].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[1].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[2].DN)XIC(Mah_Ctr[3].DN)MOV(2,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Setup MCTO with Cart_XYZRxRyRz as Cartesian System, Delta 4 axis as Robot System 
Set different work frames using Work Frame offsets array. 
Initiate MCTO with enabling “Start_MCTO” tag
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MotionGroup.GroupSynced)XIC(Start_MCTO)EQU(step,2)[MCTO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta_4_Axis,Mcto_Ctr[WorkFrame_Index],Work_Frame[WorkFrame_Index],Tool_Frame) ,XIC(Mcto_Ctr[WorkFrame_Index].IP) MOV(3,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============Start Path Moves ================
Setup MCPM with different path positions using Path_Position[] array
Move to first position as (0,0,0,180,0,0)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_PathMove)EQU(step,3)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[0],Path_Position[0],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[0].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(4,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Move to Second position as (50, 50, -100,180, 0, 0)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,4)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[1],Path_Position[1],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[1].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(5,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Move to absolute position as ( 0,  120, -100,180, 0, 30)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,5)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[2],Path_Position[2],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[2].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(6,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Move to absolute position as ( -50, 50, 0, 180, 0, -60)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,6)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[3],Path_Position[3],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[3].IP) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(7,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Move back to initial poistion as (0, 0, 0, 180, 0, 0)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,7)[MCPM(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcpm_ctr[4],Path_Position[0],1,dynamic_data,0,None) ,XIC(mcpm_ctr[4].PC) XIO(CS_XYZRxRyRz.MovePendingQueueFullStatus) MOV(8,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Update Work Frame offsets and initiate new MCTO with new work frame. 
Run the same program with updated work frames 

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,8)ADD(1,WorkFrame_Index,WorkFrame_Index)[LES(WorkFrame_Index,4) [CLR(mcpm_ctr[0].FLAGS) ,CLR(mcpm_ctr[1].FLAGS) ,CLR(mcpm_ctr[2].FLAGS) ,CLR(mcpm_ctr[3].FLAGS) ,CLR(mcpm_ctr[4].FLAGS) ,CLR(Mcto_Ctr[WorkFrame_Index].FLAGS) ] MOV(2,step) ,GEQ(WorkFrame_Index,4) MOV(10,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
Stop Cartesian  Coordinate system ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)MCS(CS_XYZRxRyRz,mcs_ctr[0],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Stop Robot Coordinate system 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSRobot)MCS(Delta_4_Axis,mcs_ctr[1],Coordinated Transform,0,0,0,0,0,0);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[=================================================================

Sample program for new Kinematics feature of Wor Frame Offsets, via MCTO programming;
Diamond shape path move u is programmed with Work Frame as a reference. Same path move is repeated for different work frames.
MCTO is programed with different Work Frame offset values.

All absolute Target positions are programmed using path positions in the MCPM instruction. 


=====  MCTO Set up  =====
Cartesian system = CS_XYZRxRyRz (6 Virtual axes, Geometry=Cartesian, Definition = XYZRxRyRz)
Robot coordinate system = Delta_4_Axis (4 Joint axes, Geometry=Delta 3D, Definition = J1J2J3J6)  
Work Frame [] = Four different offset frames are used  


================================================================

Open Trend = to view the plot of robot’s TCP Positions with and without work frames

==================================================================



]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[JSR(AbsPathMove_with_Multiple_WorkFrames,0) ,JSR(Robot_TCP_Positions,0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==========================
USER SETUP:::
Toggle bits from left to right.
===========================
Start_MCTO: Enables the Transformation between the Cartesian axes and Robot axes
Start_PathMove: Starts the robot move with different work frame references. 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTO)XIC(Start_PathMove)OTU(unlatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==================================================================


Conclusion ::
With different Work Frame offsets, User program will remain same and new TCP positions for Robot’s move will be computed by the System based on different work frame offsets

==========================
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MCSCart)XIC(MCSRobot)OTU(Stop_Program);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Robot_TCP_Positions" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Verify Robot’s TCP positions from the Robot’s Base Frame to the End of Arm using the MCTPO Forward instruction with no Work Frame offsets.  
"TCP_XY_Plot_no_WorkFrames"  shows robot’s TCP positions from the Robot's Base Frame during the MCPM moves. 
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Start_MCTO)MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[0],MCTPO_Input[0])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[1],MCTPO_Input[1])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[2],MCTPO_Input[2])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[3],MCTPO_Input[4])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[4],MCTPO_Input[4])MOV(Delta_4_Axis.ActualPosition[5],MCTPO_Input[5])CLR(mctpo_ctr.FLAGS)MCTPO(CS_XYZRxRyRz,Delta_4_Axis,mctpo_ctr,0,0,Forward,MCTPO_Input[0],MCTPO_Output,Robot_Config,Turns_Counter[0]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
